---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import { repo } from '../data/kiln';

// The latest Kiln Linux release, read from GitHub when the site builds. No release, no build:
// a deploy never ships a download link that is missing or wrong.
// Unauthenticated calls get 60 an hour per IP, and build machines share IPs: set GITHUB_TOKEN.
const token = process.env.GITHUB_TOKEN;
const res = await fetch('https://api.github.com/repos/kilnlinux/Kiln-Linux/releases/latest', {
  headers: { Accept: 'application/vnd.github+json', ...(token && { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` }) },
});
if (!res.ok) {
  const left = res.headers.get('x-ratelimit-remaining');
  throw new Error(`GitHub latest release: HTTP ${res.status}${left === '0' ? ' (rate limited; set GITHUB_TOKEN)' : ''}: ${await res.text()}`);
}
const release: {
  tag_name: string;
  published_at: string;
  body: string;
  assets: { name: string; size: number; browser_download_url: string }[];
} = await res.json();
const version = release.tag_name;
const isoAsset = release.assets.find((a) => a.name.endsWith('.iso'));
const sumAsset = release.assets.find((a) => a.name.endsWith('.iso.sha256'));
if (!isoAsset || !sumAsset) throw new Error(`${version}: release has no .iso and .iso.sha256`);
const iso = isoAsset.name;
const sha256 = (await (await fetch(sumAsset.browser_download_url)).text()).split(/\s/)[0];
if (!/^[0-9a-f]{64}$/.test(sha256)) throw new Error(`${version}: bad checksum file`);

// Bullets under a "### <heading>" in the release notes, as HTML with `code` spans.
const escape = (t: string) => t.replace(/&/g, '&amp;').replace(/</g, '&lt;').replace(/>/g, '&gt;');
const bullets = (heading: string) => {
  const section = release.body.split(/^### /m).find((b) => b.startsWith(heading + '\n') || b.startsWith(heading + '\r'));
  return (section ?? '').split(/\r?\n/).filter((l) => l.startsWith('- '))
    .map((l) => escape(l.slice(2)).replace(/`([^`]+)`/g, '<code>$1</code>'));
};
const notes = [['Tested', bullets('Tested')], ['Not tested yet', bullets('Not tested yet')]] as const;
const releaseUrl = `${repo}/releases/tag/${version}`;
const installDoc = `${repo}/blob/${version}/docs/install.md`;

// Laid out like voidlinux.org/download: prose on the left, downloads on the right.
const flavors = [
  {
    name: 'live',
    date: release.published_at.slice(0, 10),
    links: [
      { label: 'live image', href: isoAsset.browser_download_url, badge: `${(isoAsset.size / 1e9).toFixed(1)} GB` },
      { label: 'checksum', href: sumAsset.browser_download_url, badge: 'sha256' },
      { label: 'release notes', href: releaseUrl, badge: version },
    ],
  },
];
---
<Base title="Download" description={`Download Kiln Linux ${version} (beta): an x86_64 live ISO with a text installer.`}>
  <PageHeader title="Download Kiln Linux" />

  <div class="wrap space-y-3">
    <p>The <strong>live ISO</strong> is available from the GitHub releases page:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-10">
      <li><a href={`${repo}/releases`} class="link">{`${repo}/releases`}</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You need an x86_64 computer or VM with UEFI or BIOS, a disk to erase, and an internet connection during install:
      packages come from Arch’s mirrors. The <a href={installDoc} class="link">install guide</a> covers every installer
      menu item and QEMU.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section aria-labelledby="verify" class="wrap pt-8">
    <h2 id="verify" class="text-2xl">Verifying file integrity</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Check the ISO against its <a href={sumAsset.browser_download_url} class="link">checksum</a> before you use it, to
      make sure the download isn’t corrupted. In the folder with the ISO, run:
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      class="mt-4 max-w-[52rem]"
      lines={[{ in: `echo "${sha256}  ${iso}" | sha256sum -c` }, { out: `${iso}: OK` }]}
    />
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="x86_64" class="wrap pt-8">
    <ul class="flex border-b border-rule">
      <li class="-mb-px border-b-2 border-accent px-8 py-4 font-bold text-heading">x86_64</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="mt-5 grid gap-x-16 gap-y-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="min-w-0 space-y-3">
        <h2 id="x86_64" class="text-2xl">x86_64</h2>
        <p>The ISO boots on UEFI and BIOS. It is hybrid, so you can write it straight to a USB stick. Find the stick with <code>lsblk</code>; everything on it is erased.</p>
        <CodeBlock lines={[{ in: `sudo dd if=${iso} of=/dev/sdX bs=4M conv=fsync oflag=direct status=progress` }]} />
        <p>The live system logs in as <code>root</code> automatically. Ethernet comes up on its own. For Wi-Fi, run <code>iwctl</code>.</p>
        <p>
          To start the installer, run <code>kiln-install</code>. Pick the menu items in any order, then Install; it asks
          you to type the disk name before erasing it.
        </p>
        <p class="rounded-sm border border-accent px-4 py-3 font-bold">
          This is a beta: try it in a VM or on a spare disk first. Report problems as
          <a href={`${repo}/issues`} class="link">issues</a>.
        </p>
        {notes.filter(([, items]) => items.length).map(([label, items]) => (
          <div class="text-sm">
            <h3 class="label">{label}</h3>
            <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
              {items.map((item) => <li set:html={item} />)}
            </ul>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div>
        {flavors.map((f) => (
          <div class="border-b border-rule-2 pb-5 last:border-b-0">
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
              <h3 class="text-xl">{f.name}</h3>
              <small class="text-xs text-mute">{f.date}</small>
            </div>
            <ul class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2">
              {f.links.map((l) => (
                <li>
                  <a href={l.href} class="link">{l.label}</a>
                  <span class="ml-1 rounded-sm border border-accent px-1.5 py-px text-xs font-bold text-accent">{l.badge}</span>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="build" class="wrap pt-12">
    <h2 id="build" class="text-2xl">Building the ISO yourself</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      You need an x86_64 Arch Linux host. Your user needs an /etc/subuid entry, which useradd creates by default. The
      build doesn’t need root.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      class="mt-4 max-w-[52rem]"
      caption="Arch Linux host"
      lines={[
        { in: 'sudo pacman -S --needed archiso rust make' },
        { in: `git clone ${repo}.git` },
        { in: 'cd Kiln-Linux' },
        { in: 'make test' },
        { in: 'make iso' },
        { out: '# writes out/kilnlinux-YYYY.MM.DD-x86_64.iso' },
      ]}
    />
    <p class="mt-4">
      To try it in QEMU (UEFI, blank 20 GiB disk), install <code>qemu-desktop</code> and <code>edk2-ovmf</code>, then run
      <code>make run</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
